# 0091-updates-and-dlc-under-their-game.patch -- the owner's point R: updates and DLC detected automatically, shown under their base game, never as games. Applies after 0090.
# UNTESTED ON DEVICE AND IN THE SIMULATOR: compiled, and its pure part ran in the host harness (below).
#
# R. ContentSet (GameAppAttach.cs, pure): every package is a game, an update or a DLC by its title id. From the file name's tag ("[0100…800][v327680]", now also "(0100…800) (v327680)",
#    "[V65536]", any bracket after it such as "[US]" or "(14.10 GB)"), else from the PACKAGE: the cover pass (NAS, Files folders, this iPhone) now reads the content meta NCA's header
#    (*.cnmt.nca, GameIconsStream: a DLC has no control data at all) and keeps an update's or a DLC's own id in .titleids.tsv (KeepTitle: a base control NCA wins; an .xci is always a
#    game), so ContentKindOf says what it is; a name with no id is read by the NAS/Files cover pass too (it was skipped). The rules are the existing helpers' (GameAppUi.BaseTitleIdOf /
#    ContentKindOf), checked against the extractor (nx_extract opens the update as `app | 0x800`) and hactool's/nxdumptool's: base low 12 bits 000, update base | 0x800, DLC
#    AddOnContentBaseId (base + 0x1000) + index 1..0x7FF, so its base is (id - 0x1000) & ~0xFFF.
#    - Never a game of its own: the library and the Build tab list base games only (Cloud.CloudOnlyGames / PlayableGames, already; an untagged update is now recognised); under each game
#      its extras: the Library's card ("update v327680 · 2 DLC", muted, under its status), the cover flow and the iPad's hero ("On the NAS · update v327680 · 1 DLC · 20.0 GB · not on
#      this iPhone yet"), the Build tab's rows (local and cloud). A cloud game's size is its whole download (Cloud.DownloadSet: the game, its NEWEST update, all its DLC from the same
#      source, minus what this iPhone has: one download, one progress, as 0079 already did).
#    - "Updates and DLC without their game (N)": an update or DLC whose base game is nowhere (this iPhone, any cloud source), once, collapsed, "· waiting for its game", at the end of the
#      Build tab.
#    - A file that ARRIVES (Import, Open in, a folder import, Files): at the refresh of Documents each new update or DLC is said once, in the log ("content: …") and in one alert:
#      "Update v327680 attached to South Park The Fractured but Whole: rebuild to include it" (built) / "…: its build will include it" (not built) / "Update v65536 (<file>): kept, waiting
#      for its game". A download and "Add an update or DLC…" say theirs themselves (not twice). The build already takes the newest update and every DLC (UpdateFor / DlcFor); a newer
#      one makes a built game "Update available" (ContentChangedSinceBuild, 0086's "Queue a rebuild").
#    - Several updates: the newest is used; each older one is a row of the game's sheet and of the not-built sheet: "Older update v65536: remove to save 5.9 GB…" (RemoveAttached, the
#      app's own question). The log's "games found: 1 (+1 update, 0 DLC)".
#
# VERIFIED (2026-11-22, M1 Pro): check-patches-apply.sh: every patch applies in order, no fuzz, no offset; the repository's patches give exactly the compiled tree. Compile (-t:Compile):
#   0 errors / 40 warnings, the same per file and code as before 0080. Host harness (harness91: … P90;P91): 322 of 322 checks (19 new: names with and without tags, US/EU tags, [v0][US],
#   parentheses, an upper-case V, DLC ranges, an untagged update read from its package, KeepTitle, newest/older updates, the extras' lines, the cloud card, the cloud's games, the
#   download set, the orphans, the arrival words, "games found", the cover pass's reads, the wiring); 12 of 12 mutations killed.
# NOT VERIFIED: nothing ran on a device: a real content meta NCA read (NAS, Files, this iPhone), the alert at a real import, the look of the extras line and of the collapsed section.
# NEW UI STRINGS: "Updates and DLC without their game", " · waiting for its game", " attached to ", ": rebuild to include it", ": its build will include it", "): kept, waiting for its
#   game", "Older update v", ": remove to save ", "Added to its game", "Updates and DLC"; log lines "games found: ", "content: ", ": shown under its game, never as a game".
